page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="theme-color" content="#293f4a"><title>Runehaven · The Like-Terms Quest | Y7 Maths | Learning Lab</title><meta name="description" content="Create a pixel explorer, learn to collect like terms and earn treasure across six adventure worlds. A self-paced Year 7 algebra game with hints and saved progress."><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="PREFIXassets/brand/learning-lab-logo.png"><link rel="stylesheet" href="PREFIXplatform.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="PREFIXassets/brand/brand.css?v=1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="PREFIXassets/desktop-layout.css?v=desktop-1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="PREFIXassets/like-terms-rpg/game.css?v=1"><script type="module" src="PREFIXassets/like-terms-rpg/game.mjs?v=1"></script></head><body class="rpg-page"><a class="skip-link" href="#rpg-app">Skip to the adventure</a><header class="site-header"><a class="wordmark" href="PREFIXindex.html"><img class="brand-logo" src="PREFIXassets/brand/learning-lab-logo.png" width="46" height="46" alt=""><span>learning<span class="wordmark-light">lab</span><small>A PLACE FOR CURIOUS MINDS</small></span></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="../index.html">Algebra II lesson</a><a href="../prepare.html#game-like-terms-rpg">Learn the rules</a><a href="../revision.html">Revision simulator</a><a href="PREFIXactivities/games/">All games</a></nav></header><main id="main" tabindex="-1"><nav class="breadcrumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><ol><li><a href="PREFIXindex.html#/years/y7/maths">Year 7 Maths</a></li><li><a href="../index.html">Algebra II</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">The Like-Terms Quest</span></li></ol></nav><section class="rpg-hero"><div><span class="rpg-kicker">LEARN THROUGH PLAY · A PIXEL ROLE-PLAYING ADVENTURE</span><h1>Runehaven.<br>The Like-Terms Quest.</h1><p>The runes have scattered. The portals are sleeping. Create an explorer, help the guardians restore their expressions and bring six lost relics home.</p><p>Every chest holds a piece of your learning: match the letters, keep their powers and add the signed numbers.</p><div class="rpg-tags"><span>6 worlds</span><span>24 learning quests</span><span>Treasure + relics</span><span>Save and return</span></div></div><img src="PREFIXassets/like-terms-rpg/cover.svg" width="800" height="450" alt="Male and female pixel explorers beside a chest and the expression 3x + 2x = 5x"></section><section class="rpg-how" id="how-to-play"><h2>How to play</h2><ol><li><strong>Create your hero.</strong>Choose a male or female explorer, an outfit and a hero name. Add your own picture as a pixel portrait if you wish.</li><li><strong>Explore and solve.</strong>Walk using arrows or W A S D, or click a destination. Click a guardian to walk over and talk. Solve their challenge; use hints, rules and worked examples whenever you need them.</li><li><strong>Collect and advance.</strong>Walk to each unlocked chest to collect treasure. Four chests earn a relic and open the next portal. Reach the final vault by applying all the rules.</li></ol><p><b>Controls:</b> E or Space interacts with a nearby object. “Walk to my next quest” guides your explorer to the next guardian or chest. Every map destination and challenge also has buttons for keyboard use. Use Enlarge game for a bigger view.</p><p><b>Your learning, your pace:</b> there are no lives to lose or countdowns. Every completed quest earns the same treasure. Mastery stars reflect attempts and help; hints never remove coins. After studying a full solution, solve a fresh example to unlock its chest.</p><p><b>Saving and teacher results:</b> progress, character and optional portrait are saved in this browser on this device. Resume is practice. Choose “Play for my teacher” only if your teacher asks; it starts a new recorded attempt at your current level and resets that level’s four quests. Each level records separately. Hero portraits stay on this device.</p></section><details class="rpg-rules" open><summary>New to collecting like terms? Start here.</summary><div class="rpg-rule-grid"><div><h3>What are terms and variables?</h3><p>A <b>variable</b> is a letter representing a number, such as x, y or z. A <b>term</b> is one part of an expression separated by + or −. In 3x + 2y − 4, the signed terms are 3x, +2y and −4.</p><p>A <b>coefficient</b> is the number multiplying a variable part: in 3x, it is 3. A letter written alone has coefficient 1: x = 1x. Likewise, −x = −1x. A <b>constant</b> is a term without a variable, such as 5 or −4.</p></div><div><h3>What makes terms alike?</h3><p><b>Like terms</b> have exactly the same variable letters and powers. 3x and 2x are like terms; 3x and 2y are not. A <b>power</b> tells how many copies are multiplied: x² means x × x; x³ means x × x × x. The small raised number is the <b>exponent</b>.</p><p>3x² and 2x² are alike. x and x² are different families. Constants share one family. A term keeps its minus sign when you move or group it.</p></div><div><h3>Collecting adds matching quantities.</h3><p>3x + 2x means three lots of x plus two lots of x. That is five lots: <b>5x</b>. Only the coefficients add; the variable part stays the same.</p><p>4x² + 3x² = <b>7x²</b>. This adds four square terms and three square terms. It does not multiply x by x again. 3x + 2y stays <b>3x + 2y</b> because the variable parts differ.</p></div><div><h3>Keep the signs. Collect each family.</h3><p>5x − 2x + 3y + y + 4 − 1<br>= (5 − 2)x + (3 + 1)y + (4 − 1)<br>= <b>3x + 4y + 3</b>.</p><p>Terms can cancel: 3z − 3z = 0. Remove zero terms from a collected expression. You may write different families in any order: 2y + 3x is equivalent to 3x + 2y.</p></div></div></details><div id="rpg-app"><p role="status">Opening the gates of Runehaven…</p></div><noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to explore Runehaven. You can still study the rules above and the <a href="../index.html">Algebra II lesson</a>.</p></noscript><nav class="rpg-bottom-links" aria-label="Continue learning"><a href="../index.html">← Back to Algebra II</a><a href="../../algebra/games/cards.html">Play Like-Terms Recycling</a><a href="../revision.html">Try the revision simulator →</a></nav></main><footer class="site-footer"><a class="footer-brand" href="PREFIXindex.html"><img class="brand-logo" src="PREFIXassets/brand/learning-lab-logo.png" width="34" height="34" alt="">Learning Lab</a><p>Think. Build. Explain. Try again.</p><a href="PREFIXindex.html#/years/y7/maths">Year 7 Maths →</a></footer></body></html>'''.replace('PREFIX',P)
